/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (How products are presented and organized on shelves directly impacts customer perception, purchase decisions, and, ultimately, the bottom line. Effective shelf execution ensures that products are readily accessible, visually appealing, and accurately priced, fostering positive customer interactions and maximizing sales opportunities.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (However, achieving optimal shelf execution poses numerous challenges for retail teams. Ensuring that shelves adhere to planograms can be a daunting task. Managing inventory levels and ensuring stock availability on shelves can also be challenging, requiring management to invest heavily in resources to find the balance between overstocking and stockouts. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
307 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Determining and regulating the optimal placement of products on shelves to maximize visibility is a constant struggle for retail teams. Product size, packaging, and shelf positioning all contribute to influencing customer interest and buying habits. It's crucial to accurately display product prices on shelves to uphold customer trust and prevent discrepancies that may otherwise lead to customer dissatisfaction and lost sales opportunities.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
